.TH "BEEPER-LAUNCH" "1" "November 2026" "arran4/dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
beeper-launch \- prefer FlatPark Beeper with a temporary AppImage fallback
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBbeeper-launch\fR [BEEPER-ARG...]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Hyprland special-workspace configuration uses this wrapper on
session startup and for Super+B when no Beeper window is mapped.
The wrapper first checks the \fBper-user\fR Flatpak installation
of com.automattic.Beeper; if installed it starts this exact app ID
with flatpak run --user and passes any supplied arguments.
.PP
If the Flatpak is absent or launching it fails, the wrapper tries
legacy executables named beeper-appimage and beeper on PATH, then an
executable at ~/bin/beeper. This fallback is for migration only;
an old AppImage is not the preferred installation.
.PP
When no supported installation is available, the wrapper writes a
diagnostic to standard error, optionally shows a desktop notification,
and exits with status 127. No software is installed automatically.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A user-scoped Flatpak with the FlatPark remote and
com.automattic.Beeper installed is preferred. The remote registration
is a one-time operation. Beeper's runtime may additionally require
a per-user Flathub remote. See the root dotfiles README for setup.
The fallback requires an executable AppImage in a known path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
flatpak info --user com.automattic.Beeper
beeper-launch
flatpak run --user com.automattic.Beeper
command -v beeper-appimage
command -v beeper
.fi
.SH HYPRLAND INTEGRATION
Super+B toggles or activates special:beeper; it reuses an existing
window when possible and otherwise calls beeper-launch. Startup
also runs the wrapper once into that special workspace.
Known Beeper window classes are routed to special:beeper,
including com.automattic.Beeper and legacy Beeper/BeeperTexts
classes. A browser window whose title mentions Beeper should not
be captured.
.SH TROUBLESHOOTING
If no window appears, run beeper-launch in a terminal and inspect
its diagnostic output. Check the per-user installation rather than
a system-wide flatpak list. Flatpak and AppImage installations can
have different user configuration or login state.
.PP
A successful chezmoi apply does not install Beeper. The chezmoi
config template warns when the preferred FlatPark installation
is missing and provides setup instructions.
.SH SEE ALSO
hyprland-keys(7), flatpak(1)
